---
import Base from '../../../../layouts/Base.astro';
import TitleLine from '../../../../components/editorial/TitleLine.astro';
import ArticleBody from '../../../../components/editorial/ArticleBody.astro';
import Sample from '../../../../components/application-caching/style-study/Sample.astro';
import '../../../../styles/explorables.css';
import '../../../../styles/application-caching.css';

export function getStaticPaths() {
  return process.env.APPLICATION_CACHING_DRAFT_PREVIEW === '1' ? [{ params: { view: undefined } }] : [];
}
---
<Base title="One idea, three styles" description="Three visual directions for the same application-caching explanation." readingPath="/">
  <meta slot="head" name="robots" content="noindex, nofollow" />
  <article class="visual-essay cache-article" data-pagefind-ignore="all">
    <header class="essay-header">
      <p class="eyebrow">Application caching · Style study</p>
      <h1>One idea, three styles</h1>
      <TitleLine type="Introduction" />
      <p class="cache-draft-status">Working examples for choosing a visual direction.</p>
    </header>
    <ArticleBody>
      <p>Each example explains the same thing: App A reads a product’s details, builds a £20 card and saves a copy. The next request reuses that copy. There are two answers, but only one source read.</p>
      <p>Watch each version in the article’s normal typography and colours. The explanation stays fixed so the visual style is easier to compare.</p>

      <h2 id="route-map">A. The route map</h2>
      <p>A spare technical drawing. The request’s journey carries the explanation.</p>
      <Sample kind="route" number={1} />

      <h2 id="type-in-motion">B. Type in motion</h2>
      <p>An editorial treatment built from words, values and changing spacing.</p>
      <Sample kind="type" number={2} />

      <h2 id="paper-and-motion">C. Paper and motion</h2>
      <p>Flat documents make the original answer and its saved copy tangible.</p>
      <Sample kind="paper" number={3} />

      <p>These are alternatives to judge, rather than a chosen style. <a href="/review/application-caching/">Back to the application-caching article.</a></p>
      <section class="essay-sources" aria-labelledby="sources">
        <h2 id="sources">Sources and model notes</h2>
        <p>All three use the collection’s invented north-shop P7 card in English and GBP. The animation timing is illustrative. They show the cache-aside sequence described in Microsoft’s <a href="https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/architecture/patterns/cache-aside">Cache-Aside pattern</a>.</p>
      </section>
    </ArticleBody>
  </article>
</Base>
